       "text": "I haven't entered this order because 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg/day, about double the maximum daily dose of immediate-release metformin (2550 mg/day per US labeling). Metformin also doesn't come in a 1700 mg tablet (common strengths are 500, 850, and 1000 mg), so this may be a transcription or unit error.\n\nSome possibilities:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2550 mg/day, the labeled maximum for IR tablets)\n- **500 mg PO TID with meals** (1500 mg/day, a common starting or titration dose)\n- **1700 mg PO once daily** or **850 mg PO BID** (1700 mg/day), if that was the intent\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency, and I'll enter the order. Since this is a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, renal function is not a barrier to dosing, but please also confirm the indication and whether the patient is on any interacting medications."
